package sync

// Generated by `grit sync` from this project's own sync registrations. Edit
// internal/routes instead: a change here is overwritten.
//
// This is the policy table a client has before it has ever reached the server.
// Without it, the first run of a fresh install would queue a write to a
// read_only table, carry it until the next push, and show the user a failure
// that was knowable at the keystroke (grit#214).
//
// It is a bootstrap and not the authority. GET /sync/policy replaces every
// entry here as soon as the device syncs once, and the result is persisted, so
// this file only ever matters before the first successful sync and after a
// reinstall. A table absent from it is offline_first, which is why generating
// a resource does not break the desktop app until somebody runs grit sync.

// bootstrapPolicies is keyed by table name.
var bootstrapPolicies = map[string]Policy{
	// grit:sync-policies
}
